mod backend.optimizer.passes.removal;

import (
    std.io,
    backend.finalizer.ir
)

/**
 * THE PASSES THAT REMOVE: code whose work nobody sees
 *
 * Generated code is full of values made "just in case" - a constant loaded
 * into a slot it is copied out of, a result nobody takes - and the value
 * passes (passes/values) leave more of them behind each time they make a
 * copy or a constant unnecessary. These passes take them away. They never
 * remove anything the program can see: a store into a field or an element,
 * a call, a jump, a return, anything that may raise an exception
 * (analysis/instruction_facts.sharp, `has_effect`).
 *
 * The files of this package (module `backend.optimizer.passes.removal`):
 *
 *      removal.sharp               this front door
 *      dead_stores.sharp           a value written where nobody reads it again (liveness)
 *      dead_objects.sharp          an object that is made and filled but never read is not made
 *      dead_code.sharp             values that only feed themselves ("mark and sweep")
 *      unreachable_code.sharp      code control can never come to
 */
